---
source: crates/news/tests/cli.rs
expression: "stdout_of(&[\"jobs\", \"--help\"])"
---
Dispatch: the job queue

Usage: news jobs [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list       Counts by pool and state, and recent jobs
  dead       Discarded jobs grouped by error class and message
  claim      Claim ready jobs from a pool (Ghost); --limit sets how many
  heartbeat  Extend a running job's lease
  complete   Mark a running job completed
  fail       Record a failure; the error class decides retry, snooze or discard
  retry      Re-enqueue a discarded job, or every discarded job of a class
  pause      Pause a pool (H tier)
  unpause    Unpause a pool (H tier)
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --limit <N>        Return at most N list items (default 20; `jobs claim`: how many to claim, default 1)
      --fields <A,B>     Keep only these keys of each item, comma-separated
      --cursor <CURSOR>  Continue a truncated list from its next_cursor
  -h, --help             Print help
